  "portal_description": "The Eclipse platform is designed for building integrated development\nenvironments (IDEs), server-side applications, desktop applications, and\neverything in between. The devtoolset-3-eclipse packages provide the Red Hat\nDeveloper Toolset version of Eclipse.\n\nThis enhancement update adds the devtoolset-3-eclipse packages to Red Hat\nDeveloper Toolset 3.0 for Red Hat Enterprise Linux. These packages are based on\nEclipse Luna simultaneous release train, which is the latest one, and are based\non Eclipse Platform 4.4.0. This release provides numerous new features, bug\nfixes, and optimizations over the previous version included in Red Hat Developer\nToolset 2.1. Additionally: \n\n* The devtoolset-3-eclipse-cdt packages, which contain Eclipse CDT (C/C++\nDevelopment Tooling), have been upgraded to version 8.5.0.\n* The devtoolset-3-eclipse-mylyn packages, which contain the Mylyn\ntask-management subsystem, have been upgraded to version 3.12.0.\n* The devtoolset-3-eclipse-linuxtools packages, which contain the Eclipse Linux\nTools plug-in collection, have been upgraded to version 3.1.0.\n* The devtoolset-3-eclipse-egit packages, which contain a Git integration\nplug-in for Eclipse, have been upgraded to version 3.4.1.\n* The devtoolset-3-eclipse-jgit packages, which contain a Java library\nimplementing Git, have been upgraded to version 3.4.1. \n(BZ#1100853, BZ#1142461, BZ#1142464)\n\nAll users who require devtoolset-3-eclipse are advised to install these new\npackages.\n",
